<title>BELGIUM: EU clears Swedish state aid shipping scheme.</title>
<headline>EU clears Swedish state aid shipping scheme.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission cleared on Wednesday a Swedish state scheme to aid shipping with a total budget of 400 million crowns for 1997.</p>
<p>The scheme is designed to help maintain and enhance employment opportunities and training places on board Swedish flagged vessels operating in international cargo trades to or from Sweden.</p>
<p>The scheme, an extension of one already in place since 1994, will run until the end of 2001.</p>
<p>&quot;The Commission found the scheme compatible with European Union law and in line with its policy designed to counter the flagging out trend, to promote employment of EU seafarers and on-board training,&quot; the Commission said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
